## 2. Arm means by slot

| Arm | Slot A, pilot, one assay a run | Slot A, part A, three a run | Slot B, part A, three a run |
|---|---|---|---|
| twin-free-rival | +0.263 | +0.183 | +0.240 |
| twin-free-collective | +0.020 | +0.201 | +0.369 |
| twin-stack-collective | +0.199 | +0.146 | +0.166 |
| solo-pair | +0.492 | +0.429 | +0.314 |
| twin-fixed-builder | +0.474 | +0.452 | +0.360 |

The planned contrasts on slot A alone, part A's assays: free minus solo -0.228 (exact p 0.2000), free minus seed builder -0.251 (exact p 0.1429). Chosen after seeing the data, so not a test of anything.

## 3. How much one assay says about a harness

36 distinct harnesses (assays each: 3: 32, 6: 3, 12: 1), 126 assays. Between-harness variance 0.0300 (SD 0.173), between-assay variance within a harness 0.0292 (SD 0.171).
Intraclass correlation 0.507. Reliability of a harness's mean gain over k assays (Spearman-Brown): k=1: 0.51, k=3: 0.76, k=6: 0.86, k=12: 0.93.

## 4. No edit: a trait of the harness or chance each time

Pooled no-edit rate over built harnesses 0.237. Harnesses with three assays: 32.

| No-edit assays of 3 | Harnesses | Expected if every harness had the pooled rate |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 24 | 14.2 |
| 1 | 4 | 13.2 |
| 2 | 0 | 4.1 |
| 3 | 4 | 0.4 |

